fman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7792","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7792"}},{"id":"7793","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5553","description":"Tor and Kevin at the top of the first drop below Coyote Falls.","caption":"South Fork - Below Coyote Falls","poi_name":"","subject":"Tor Andersen and Kevin Pickens","author":"Todd Hoffman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7793","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7793"}},{"id":"7794","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5553","description":"Tor and Kevin putting in below Coyote Falls.","caption":"South Fork - Put in","poi_name":"","subject":"Tor Andersen and Kevin Pickens","author":"Todd Hoffman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7794","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7794"}},{"id":"7795","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5553","description":"Approaching the second major drop after Coyote Falls.","caption":"South Fork - Second Drop","poi_name":"","subject":"Kevin Pickens and Tor Andersen","author":"Todd Hoffman","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7795","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7795"}},{"id":"11415","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6737","description":"","caption":"lower rawlings...","poi_name":"Rawlings","subject":"Brian Mattingly","author":"Jon Crane","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11415","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11415"}},{"id":"11416","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6737","description":"","caption":"fish jump...","poi_name":"Fish Jump","subject":"salmon","author":"Brian Mattingly","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11416","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11416"}},{"id":"13872","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7709","description":"","caption":"Ranier Rob and Shane 54 rollin'","poi_name":"","subject":"Rob Lee and Shane Wilhite","author":"Russel the Muscle","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13872","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13872"}},{"id":"11975","ext":"bmp","post_id":"7710","description":"","caption":"The calm before the storm","poi_name":"","subject":"Rob Lee, Shane Wilhite and Brian Lee","author":"?","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11975","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11975"}}],"detail":{"id":"544","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Flows between 2,000 and 4,000 the run offers fun continuous class 4-5 rapids with 3 stand out solid class 5 rapids. From around 1000 up to 2000 the river is more on the class IV side but remains a challenging run with somewhat technical moves and plenty of punch. Above 4,000 golden canyon becomes one of the best class 5 big water runs in the states. It is navagable at flows upwards of 8,000 by solid class 5 kayakers. The road is along the river for scouting and portaging. Shorter runs are possible.\n\n**Description:**\n\nThe run begins at Hanging Rock (MP 28). You will know it when you see it. The mile upstream is Coyote Falls and should be scouted just to marvel at it. Coyote Falls is 0.3 miles of terror and 0.7 miles of IV+ at low flows. From Hanging Rock down are three miles of continuous rock dodging. You may wish to portage Chuck Rollins at mile post 25.4. This is followed by two miles of easy water. Then, the action picks up again for another two miles. You may wish to portage Fish Jump at mile post 22.4. Take out at Cougar Creek Trailhead about Âmile post 20.6. The next 6.8 miles are class II with a few easy class IIIs. Check out the [Mickey Mouse](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=2173) run if the water here is too high for you.\n\n**Shuttle:** [Road Map](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=2173)\n\nTo get to the take-out: Go up Idaho State Highway 14 to Cougar Creek Trailhead around road mile 20.6. Park at the trailhead. It's free.\n\nTo get to the put-in: Go upstream 7.4 miles to MP 28 and park in the wide spot upstream of the hanging rock. Stop at Fish Jump, two miles upstream (mile 22.4) and Chuck Rollins, five upstream (mile 25.4) to scout.","averageGradient":"85","maxGradient":null,"length":"7.2","correlations":[{"reachID":"544","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"800","beginMediumRunnable":"1200","beginHighRunnable":"2300","endHighRunnable":"3500"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"SF CLEARWATER RIVER AT STITES ID","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"13338500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"1450","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"4.26","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"46.08638889","longitude":"-115.9766667"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/13338500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/13338500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"medium-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"1450","da